{#
  Family box for the record sidebar.

  _layouts/base.twig hands this partial a `fam` of parents, children, siblings,
  spouses and other relations, already de-duplicated, with the record itself
  removed, and with every kinship row already limited to stored relations
  between two historical people. That is shared with the JSON-LD, so the box and
  the graph can never disagree. Nothing here is derived: no grandparents, no
  grandchildren, no siblings from shared parents.

  The box renders only when something resolves, and each row renders only when
  that relation has someone in it, so an unrecorded family costs nothing on the
  page. Same two conditional rules as every other box on a record.

  Each row is built like the Related person box it replaces: a 56px circular
  portrait, the name in Playfair, and the occupation or the dates beneath in the
  muted grey. Where a record has no featuredImage the circle is cream with a
  gold border and the person's initials, so every row has the same footprint and
  an absent portrait reads as deliberate rather than broken.

  Other relations is whatever wmRelatedPerson, relatedPersons or mpRelatedPersons
  held that is not already a parent, child, sibling or spouse. The
  separate Related person box is retired: a family member is a related person,
  and two boxes for one relationship is noise.

  Dates and occupation come from whichever handles the related record's own
  layout carries: a person keeps birthDate, deathDate and occupation, a casualty
  keeps wmDateOfBirth and wmRank. The handle is looked for in the layout rather
  than probed with `is defined`, which answers true for a field the type does
  not have.

  A LIVING PERSON IS A NAME. Anyone who fails the historical test in
  _partials/record/historical.twig (undetermined counts as living) is listed by
  name alone, behind the initials circle: no portrait, no occupation, no birth
  year. They are not the subject of this page, and a birth year is a routine
  identity-verification field. Kinship rows never reach here with a living
  person in them; this covers Other relations, and holds whatever the caller
  hands in.

  Params
    fam  the derived family, or null
#}
{% import "_partials/record/historical" as hist %}
{% if fam %}
  {% set rows = [
    ['PARENTS', fam.parents],
    ['CHILDREN', fam.children],
    ['SIBLINGS', fam.siblings],
    ['SPOUSE', fam.spouses],
    ['OTHER RELATIONS', fam.other ?? []]
  ]|filter(r => r[1]|length) %}
  {#- The box says FAMILY only when it holds kinship. Other relations are
      curated links, not kinship claims, and a curated link to a living person
      under a FAMILY heading would state the family structure the kinship rule
      has just withheld. Alone, they are RELATED PEOPLE, with no row label. -#}
  {% set kinRows = rows|filter(r => r[0] != 'OTHER RELATIONS') %}

  {% if rows|length %}
    {% css %}
    .rec-fam{margin:0}
    .rec-fam .lab{font-family:'Jost',sans-serif;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A5C1B;margin:14px 0 2px}
    .rec-fam .lab:first-child{margin-top:0}
    .rec-fam a.p{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:center;color:inherit;text-decoration:none;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #EFE6D0}
    .rec-fam a.p:last-child{border-bottom:0}
    .rec-fam .th{width:56px;height:56px;border-radius:50%;flex:none;overflow:hidden;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:#EEF0F4}
    .rec-fam .th img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover}
    .rec-fam .th.ini{background:#FDF7EA;border:1px solid #C4A031;font-family:'Jost',sans-serif;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:#7A5C1B}
    .rec-fam .n{font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.3;color:#17254C}
    .rec-fam a.p:hover .n{color:#7A5C1B}
    .rec-fam .r{font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;color:#5B6472;margin-top:2px}
    .rec-fam .wm{display:inline-block;font-family:'Jost',sans-serif;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A5C1B;background:#FDF7EA;border:1px solid #EFE6D0;padding:1px 6px;margin-top:4px}
    {% endcss %}

    <div class="rec-box">
      <div class="rec-lab">{{ kinRows|length ? 'FAMILY' : 'RELATED PEOPLE' }}</div>
      <div class="rec-fam">
        {% for row in rows %}
          {% if kinRows|length %}<div class="lab">{{ row[0] }}</div>{% endif %}
          {% for p in row[1] %}
            {% set living = not (hist.historical(p)|trim) %}
            {% set ph = [] %}
            {% for f in (p.fieldLayout ? p.fieldLayout.customFields : []) %}{% set ph = ph|merge([f.handle]) %}{% endfor %}

            {% set born = 'birthDate' in ph ? p.birthDate : ('wmDateOfBirth' in ph ? p.wmDateOfBirth : ('mpDateOfBirth' in ph ? p.mpDateOfBirth : '')) %}
            {% set died = 'deathDate' in ph ? p.deathDate : ('mpDateOfDeath' in ph ? p.mpDateOfDeath : '') %}
            {% set b = born|trim ? born|trim|slice(-4) : '' %}
            {% set d = died|trim ? died|trim|slice(-4) : '' %}
            {% set span = (b matches '/^\\d{4}$/' or d matches '/^\\d{4}$/')
              ? ((b matches '/^\\d{4}$/' ? b : '') ~ '–' ~ (d matches '/^\\d{4}$/' ? d : '')) : '' %}

            {# Occupation where the record keeps one, the dates otherwise, so the
               second line says whatever that record actually knows. #}
            {% set role = 'occupation' in ph ? p.occupation|trim : ('wmRank' in ph ? p.wmRank|trim : ('mpRank' in ph ? p.mpRank|trim : '')) %}
            {% set sub = role ?: span %}
            {% if role and span %}{% set sub = role ~ ' · ' ~ span %}{% endif %}
            {% if living %}{% set sub = '' %}{% endif %}

            {% set img = not living and 'featuredImage' in ph ? p.featuredImage.one() ?? null : null %}
            {% set words = (p.title ?: p.slug)|trim|split(' ')|filter(w => w|trim) %}
            {% set ini = (words|first|slice(0, 1) ~ (words|length > 1 ? words|last|slice(0, 1) : ''))|upper %}

            <a class="p" href="{{ p.url }}">
              {% if img %}
                <div class="th"><img src="{{ img.url }}" alt=""></div>
              {% else %}
                <div class="th ini" aria-hidden="true">{{ ini }}</div>
              {% endif %}
              <div style="min-width:0">
                <div class="n">{{ p.title ?: p.slug }}</div>
                {% if sub %}<div class="r">{{ sub }}</div>{% endif %}
                {#- The badge marks a family member who is themselves a casualty
                    record. It used to ask which war memorial pointed AT them,
                    which on a casualty's own page found that page and put a
                    badge on their father linking back to the son. -#}
                {% if p.section.handle == 'warMemorials' %}<div class="wm">War Memorial</div>{% endif %}
              </div>
            </a>
          {% endfor %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
